/// <p>There are two ways to construct an item group. The easiest and most common approach is to pass a list of items (e.g., all selected items) to <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qgraphicsscene.html#createItemGroup" translate="no">QGraphicsScene::createItemGroup</a>(), which returns a new QGraphicsItemGroup item. The other approach is to manually construct a QGraphicsItemGroup item, add it to the scene calling <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qgraphicsscene.html#addItem" translate="no">QGraphicsScene::addItem</a>(), and then add items to the group manually, one at a time by calling <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qgraphicsitemgroup.html#addToGroup" translate="no">addToGroup</a>(). To dismantle ("ungroup") an item group, you can either call <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qgraphicsscene.html#destroyItemGroup" translate="no">QGraphicsScene::destroyItemGroup</a>(), or you can manually remove all items from the group by calling <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qgraphicsitemgroup.html#removeFromGroup" translate="no">removeFromGroup</a>().</p>
