/// <p><b>Note: </b><a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qwidget.html" translate="no">QWidget</a>-based widgets can be directly embedded into a <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qgraphicsscene.html" translate="no">QGraphicsScene</a> using <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qgraphicsproxywidget.html" translate="no">QGraphicsProxyWidget</a>.</p>
/// </div>
/// <p>Noticeable differences between QGraphicsWidget and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qwidget.html" translate="no">QWidget</a> are:</p>
/// <div class="table"><table class="generic">
///  <thead><tr class="qt-style"><th>QGraphicsWidget</th><th><a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qwidget.html" translate="no">QWidget</a></th></tr></thead>
/// <tbody><tr valign="top" class="odd"><td>Coordinates and geometry are defined with qreals (doubles or floats, depending on the platform).</td><td><a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qwidget.html" translate="no">QWidget</a> uses integer geometry (<a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qpoint.html" translate="no">QPoint</a>, <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qrect.html" translate="no">QRect</a>).</td></tr>
