/// <p>QRhiWidget provides functionality for displaying 3D content rendered through the <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qrhi.html" translate="no">QRhi</a> APIs within a <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qwidget.html" translate="no">QWidget</a>-based application. In many ways it is the portable equivalent of <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qopenglwidget.html" translate="no">QOpenGLWidget</a> that is not tied to a single 3D graphics API, but rather can function with all the APIs <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qrhi.html" translate="no">QRhi</a> supports (such as, Direct 3D 11/12, Vulkan, Metal, and OpenGL).</p>
