/// <p>If you want to navigate through all the (key, value) pairs stored in a QMap, you can use an iterator. QMap provides both <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/java-style-iterators.html#java-style-iterators">Java-style iterators</a> (<a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qmapiterator.html" translate="no">QMapIterator</a> and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qmutablemapiterator.html" translate="no">QMutableMapIterator</a>) and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/containers.html#stl-style-iterators">STL-style iterators</a> (<a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qmap-const-iterator.html" translate="no">QMap::const_iterator</a> and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qmap-iterator.html" translate="no">QMap::iterator</a>). Here's how to iterate over a QMap&lt;<a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qstring.html" translate="no">QString</a>, int&gt; using a Java-style iterator:</p>
